--    inside a CTE. The T-SQL detour through a table variable exists only because SQL Server
--    rejects a bare OUTPUT on a table with enabled triggers (error 334, noted in the original);
--    PostgreSQL has no such restriction, and RETURNING keeps the property that matters -- it is
--    still ONE atomic UPDATE, never select-then-update, so zero rows returned still means
--    "you lost, do not proceed".
--
